---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/content/FaqList.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Does the website make network requests?',
    answer:
      'Yes. Opening a website normally requests its HTML, styles, scripts, icons, and other assets from a host. The privacy boundary is that WorkoutMatch application code does not send your workout inputs, calculator values, or locally saved history to a server.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Is locally saved data automatically backed up?',
    answer:
      'No. Browser data can be cleared, blocked, become unavailable, or stay only on one device and browser profile. Use the explicit JSON export if you want a copy you control.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can another person using my browser see my progress?',
    answer:
      'Potentially, yes. People with access to the same device and browser profile may be able to view locally saved progress or downloaded exports.',
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy: On-Device Workout and Calculator Data"
  description="Learn which ordinary website requests occur, which WorkoutMatch inputs stay on your device, what is stored locally, and how exports and browser clearing work."
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />
  </div>

  <header class="narrow section-sm">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language data boundaries</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The initial WorkoutMatch application has no account, backend, or cloud
      sync. Workout inputs, calculator values, and locally saved progress are
      processed on your device and are not sent to a server by application code.
    </p>
  </header>

  <article class="narrow privacy-content">
    <section class="request-grid" aria-labelledby="requests-heading">
      <h2 id="requests-heading">Website requests and app data are different</h2>
      <div class="grid-cards">
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <p class="eyebrow">Normal asset requests</p>
          <h3>What loading the site requires</h3>
          <p>
            Your browser ordinarily requests page HTML, compiled CSS and
            JavaScript, icons, and other self-hosted assets. The host and
            network providers may receive routine request information such as an
            IP address, date and time, requested path, browser headers, and
            referrer according to their own infrastructure and policies.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <p class="eyebrow">On-device application data</p>
          <h3>What the app keeps local</h3>
          <p>
            Generator selections, movement preferences, calculator inputs and
            results, workout records, saved plans, and import contents are
            handled in the browser. WorkoutMatch application code does not
            transmit those values to a server, analytics service, ad system, or
            error reporter.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="callout">
        WorkoutMatch does not claim “zero network requests.” The accurate
        promise is narrower: personal workout and calculator data are processed
        on the device and are not transmitted by application code.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage-heading">
      <h2 id="storage-heading">What can be stored in your browser</h2>
      <dl class="data-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Theme and small preferences</dt>
          <dd>
            An explicit light/dark theme override, preferred units, and optional
            generator defaults can use localStorage.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Saved workouts and history</dt>
          <dd>
            When you choose to save, IndexedDB can hold workout dates,
            exercises, completion or skip status, sets, repetitions, duration,
            optional weights, and saved plans.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Calculator values</dt>
          <dd>
            Measurements, age, equation choice, and results are not stored by
            default. Only an explicit “remember my units” preference may
            persist.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Theme before page display</dt>
          <dd>
            A small self-hosted script reads the saved theme choice early so the
            page does not flash the wrong theme.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p>
        Local storage is not private from everyone who can use the same browser
        profile. It can also be blocked, cleared automatically, removed by you,
        or lost when a device fails. No automatic backup or cross-device
        synchronization is provided.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="urls-heading">
      <h2 id="urls-heading">URLs, sharing, and printouts</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy-safe workout sharing may encode an allowlisted, non-sensitive
        generator configuration and versioned seed in a URL. It must not include
        movement sensitivities, calculator inputs or results, local workout
        records, notes, filenames, or imported data. Review a link before
        sending it because anyone who receives a URL can copy or retain it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Printing or saving a printout moves information outside WorkoutMatch
        storage controls. Shared devices, browser print history, downloaded
        PDFs, and physical pages should be handled according to your own privacy
        needs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="exports-heading">
      <h2 id="exports-heading">Export, import, and clear controls</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Export creates a JSON file from local saved plans, progress, and
          preferences only when you request it.
        </li>
        <li>
          That downloaded file is no longer protected by browser storage. Anyone
          with file access may be able to read it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Import reads a selected file on the device, validates its structure
          and size, and shows a preview before merge or replacement.
        </li>
        <li>
          Replacing or clearing local data requires confirmation because the app
          cannot restore information that was not exported.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}my-progress/`}>Open My progress</a> to
        manage browser-stored workout data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="third-parties-heading">
      <h2 id="third-parties-heading">Third parties and future changes</h2>
      <p>
        The initial application does not load analytics, an ad network, social
        embeds, or third-party fonts. Advertisement layout zones are disabled
        and do not show fake ads. If analytics, advertising, crash reporting, or
        another third party is enabled later, it requires a deliberate privacy,
        consent, security, and performance review. It must not receive generator
        constraints, movement sensitivities, calculator values, local history,
        import contents, or free-text notes.
      </p>
      <p>
        A deployment host has its own operational logging and retention
        practices, which are outside this code’s on-device storage controls.
        This page should be updated when a real host or approved third party
        changes those facts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="choices-heading">
      <h2 id="choices-heading">Your practical choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the generator and calculators without saving results.</li>
        <li>
          Decline persistent preferences by leaving theme and unit choices at
          their defaults.
        </li>
        <li>
          Export a local copy before clearing browser data, if you want to keep
          it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Use browser or site controls to clear locally saved WorkoutMatch data.
        </li>
        <li>
          Avoid saving on a shared browser profile if other people should not
          see the records.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>

  <div class="narrow section-sm">
    <FaqList items={faqs} heading="Privacy questions" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-content > section + section {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .privacy-content p,
  .privacy-content li,
  .privacy-content dd {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .privacy-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
  }

  .request-grid > h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }

  .request-grid article p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .request-grid .callout {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .data-list {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .data-list div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .data-list dt {
    font-weight: 780;
  }

  .data-list dd {
    margin: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 42rem) {
    .data-list div {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 0.45fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
